    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WPI_External_Career_Site/job/Worcester/Administrative-Specialist_R0003805": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Administrative Specialist LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Integrative & Global Studies DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Administrative Specialist in the Department of Integrative and Global Studies (DIGS) is an organizational anchor who unites and supports a dynamic department community. With about 30 full-time faculty, numerous adjunct and affiliated faculty, and staff collaborators in offices across campus, DIGS helps deliver WPI’s unique experiential learning programs. Faculty and staff bring a commitment to community-engagement and global and intercultural learning, to help students grow as future leaders and ethical practitioners. The Administrative Specialist supports the operations and activities of this community-minded and growth-oriented department. JOB DESCRIPTION Responsibilities: Provide comprehensive administrative support to the department head, program directors, faculty, staff, and department committees. Manage confidential records and documents, coordinate meetings and calendars, prepare agendas and meeting notes, and support departmental communications and initiatives. Assist with departmental events and meetings, including scheduling, space reservations, catering, guest arrangements, flyers, and announcements. Support faculty searches and other academic processes, including candidate correspondence, interview scheduling, visitor arrangements, and related documentation. Share responsibility for supervising student workers and supporting various department initiatives. Provide administrative and financial support, including processing expense reports and  assisting with financial reporting. Support departmental outreach and communications in collaboration with Marketing and Communications. Maintain and update department websites using content management systems such as Drupal and WordPress, and maintain signage, announcements, and displays. Research and develop content for newsletters, websites, and social media, including short features highlighting department projects and activities. Coordinate general office operations, including conference room calendars, facilities work orders, shared office equipment, supplies, and mail. Provide a welcoming and supporting atmosphere, and generally serve as a resource to, faculty, staff, students, and visitors.   Requirements:  High school degree or GED. Some college or university is a plus. 3 years of experience in an administrative or office setting. Excellent communication and computer skills are required. Proficiency using Microsoft tools and have the ability and willingness to learn new computer skills and adapt to changing job requirements. High level of judgment and confidentiality, and the ability to interact effectively with a wide range of people. Ability to work independently as well as part of a team. To Apply: Please submit a cover letter and resume for consideration. Compensation: Hourly pay rate: $23.00 - $25.50 per hour. Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity.  WPI’s benefits package includes a robust retirement match, wellness perks, tuition assistance and more! FLSA STATUS United States of America (Non-Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WPI_External_Career_Site/job/Worcester/Counselor_R0003770": {
      "title": "Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Counselor LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Student Development & Counseling Center - SDCC DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Counselor provides counseling, assessment, consultation, crisis intervention, outreach referrals, and programming to support the emotional health and personal growth of WPI students. The Counselor is a collaborative team player who pursues a deepening understanding of the intersectional identities of all members of our WPI community, while providing education and guidance to staff, faculty, parents, student leaders, and other campus partners. The Counselor leads with strong ethical standards and excellent problem-solving, interpersonal, and communication skills. This is a 10-month position. JOB DESCRIPTION Responsibilities: Provide high-quality counseling services to WPI students by: Offering short-term individual, group, and couples counseling, crisis intervention, and outreach referrals Conducting alcohol and other drug assessments mandated by the Dean of Students office Maintaining schedule and timely clinical records and notes through the HIPAA-compliant Titanium record system Providing crisis intervention, consultation, and assessment as needed Serving as after-hours on-call clinician in weekly rotation Providing support to the WPI community in the event of a critical incident Support specific program activities and initiatives through: Working in coordination with other campus offices and student groups on campus to design, market, and provide outreach programming on topics related to mental health, emotional growth, and personal development Participating in Division of Student Affairs and Campus Life meetings and activities, including events organized by other campus partners to support the WPI community Serving on Division or Campus-Wide committees as appropriate Assisting in the selection and training of interns Providing peer supervision, clinical case consultation, and training to interns and other professional staff within the Student Development and Counseling Center Participating in the Worcester Consortium Counselors meetings as scheduled Attending relevant conferences and staying abreast of trends in higher education, particularly pertaining to student life, mental health, and well-being Engage in case management to connect students with appropriate levels of care by: Facilitating referrals to support staff in other offices at WPI Negotiating clinical coordination, referrals, and consultation with outpatient providers as appropriate Supporting students in outreach with campus partners Collaborating with the Clinical Case Manager to develop and maintain a clinical resource library Administer consulting and outreach programming by: Consulting and collaborating with students, staff, faculty, and parents to best support the mental health and well-being of WPI students Serving as liaison to Student Affinity Spaces Serving as advisor and providing consultation for relevant student organizations, including but not limited to SPARC (Students Preventing Assault and Rape in our Community), SMART, and Active Minds Performs all other duties and responsibilities as assigned or directed by the supervisor. Qualifications: Master's Degree in Counselor Education, Counseling Psychology, Mental Health Counseling, Social Work, Higher Education Counseling, or Clinical Psychology required License-eligible as a Mental Health Counselor, Psychologist, or Social Worker in the State of Massachusetts 1 year of experience Demonstrates ability and willingness to work with a diverse population of students in individual, group, and programming settings Adaptable, creative, and able to thrive in a collaborative team environment Experience working in a college counseling environment preferred Skills, knowledge, and experience specifically focused on the needs of students of color, students from indigenous communities, LGBTQIA+ students, international students, first-generation students, and students holding other intersectional identities Experience in goal-focused individual and group therapy models (DBT, ACT, Solution-Focused Therapy, CBT) College mental health experience preferred Salary Grade 6: $52,000 – $56,000 per year (depending on experience) Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range.  Compensation at WPI FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WPI_External_Career_Site/job/Worcester/Assistant-Professor---Mechanical-and-Materials-Engineering---Soft-Materials_R0003807": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor | Mechanical and Materials Engineering - Soft Materials",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Assistant Professor | Mechanical and Materials Engineering - Soft Materials LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Mechanical & Materials Engineering DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Mechanical and Materials Engineering Department at Worcester Polytechnic Institute (WPI) seeks applicants for a tenure-track faculty position in the area of Soft Materials available at the assistant professor level. The successful candidate will possess a strong background in soft materials and demonstrate excellence in research and teaching related to the design, processing, characterization, and application of soft matter systems. Areas of expertise may include, but are not limited to, polymers, elastomers, gels, colloids, biomaterials, functional soft materials, stimuli-responsive materials, sustainable materials, soft composites, materials for energy and environmental applications, and advanced characterization and modeling of soft matter. Research that integrates materials design with emerging approaches such as artificial intelligence, machine learning, data-driven materials discovery, advanced manufacturing, or multiscale modeling is particularly welcome. Applications may span areas such as healthcare and biomedical technologies, energy storage and conversion, sustainable materials and circular economy, soft robotics, wearable and flexible electronics, advanced manufacturing, and other areas complementary to the department's existing strengths. A demonstrated ability to develop innovative, multidisciplinary research programs addressing important societal challenges is highly desirable. The candidate will be expected to develop an active externally funded research program and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in materials science and engineering, mechanical engineering, and related areas. Candidates must possess a PhD or equivalent degree in materials science and engineering, mechanical engineering, chemical engineering, polymer science, or a closely related discipline. This position is expected to be filled at the Assistant Professor level. For experienced candidates, rank will be commensurate with experience. JOB DESCRIPTION The Mechanical and Materials Engineering Department at WPI (https://www.wpi.edu/academics/departments/mechanical-materials-engineering) has 25 dual-mission faculty, 8 full-time teaching faculty, and 13 research faculty.  MME offers undergraduate degrees in mechanical engineering to over 1200 students. The department offers graduate degrees in mechanical engineering, materials science and engineering, and manufacturing engineering to about 200 graduate students. The department’s annual externally sponsored research expenditures have exceeded $19.7M. WPI’s reputation as a rigorous and innovative university rests on the shoulders of its faculty. A highly selective, private technological university and one of the nation’s first, WPI believes that when great minds work together, great advances follow. At WPI the boundaries to multidisciplinary collaboration are low—faculty members, students, and other partners work together on the real-world projects and purposeful research that are hallmarks of the WPI experience. Located one hour west of Boston, the university’s campus is in Worcester, Massachusetts, a thriving 21st century college city recognized as a growing hub of scientific and technological innovation. To Apply: Applications should include curriculum vitae, statements of teaching and research interests, and a list of five professional references. This search will remain open until the position is filled. Questions can be addressed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Professor Jianyu Liang, jianyul@wpi.edu. Compensation: Salary: $105,000 - $110,000 per year.  Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity.  WPI’s benefits package includes a robust retirement match, wellness perks, tuition assistance and more! FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WPI_External_Career_Site/job/Worcester/MME-Graduate-Administrative-Associate_R0003793": {
      "title": "Administrative Associate",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Administrative Associate LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Mechanical & Materials Engineering DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Graduate Administrative Associate is primarily responsible for the support of the Mechanical and Materials Engineering (MME) Department's Bachelor's/Master’s (BS/MS), Masters (MS), and PhD students from acceptance through graduation. Involved at many levels in the support of the department’s Teaching Assistants and Research Assistants. Responsible for hourly undergraduate and graduate student payroll, including hiring, timesheet approval, and running reports as requested by the department. Assist the operations manager and faculty with the preparation and electronic storage of Accreditation Board for Engineering and Technology (ABET) materials for the Mechanical and Materials Engineering Program. JOB DESCRIPTION Responsibilities: Provide comprehensive administrative support for the Mechanical Engineering graduate programs, working closely with the Mechanical Engineering Graduate Committee (MEGC), Graduate Coordinator, faculty, and students. Support BS/MS, MS, and PhD students from admission through graduation; maintain graduate student records and reports; coordinate qualifying exams, thesis proposals and defenses, degree completion processes, graduate seminars, and textbook orders. Support the administration of teaching and research assistantships, including quarterly TA assignments, RA/TA payments, TA evaluations, and related reporting. Manage hourly undergraduate and graduate student employment, including hiring, timesheets, payroll, costing allocations, and student worker schedules. Participate in the annual Federal Work-Study Job Fair and supervise student office workers. Coordinate department events and activities, including TA and graduate student meetings, BS/MS and PhD information sessions, luncheons, celebrations, and the annual prospective PhD student visitation retreat. Manage room reservations and event logistics using 25Live and other campus resources. Provide day-to-day administrative support to the Department Head, faculty, students, staff, and visitors. Manage calendars and meetings, respond to departmental inquiries, coordinate office and laboratory access, submit facilities and IT requests, process Workday expense reports, and assist with new faculty office setup and visiting international student access. Order departmental supplies, apparel, and gifts, and provide backup support to other department administrative staff. Participate in and provide administrative support for department and university meetings, including the Mechanical Engineering Graduate Committee, Graduate Administrator meetings, Costing Allocation meetings, and Affinity Group meetings. Meet regularly with the Graduate Coordinator to coordinate priorities, assignments, and follow-up activities. Requirements: High school degree or GED. 3 years of experience in an administrative or office setting. Excellent communication and computer skills are required. Proficiency using Excel, Word, and PowerPoint and have the ability and willingness to learn new computer skills and adapt to changing job requirements. High level of judgment and confidentiality, and the ability to interact effectively with a wide range of people.  Ability to work independently as well as part of a team. To Apply: Please attach a cover letter and resume for consideration. Compensation: Hourly pay rate: $21.25 - $25.00 per hour.  Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity.  WPI’s benefits package includes a robust retirement match, wellness perks, tuition assistance and more! FLSA STATUS United States of America (Non-Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
